# Pickled Red Onions

Based on [https://newsletter.ethanchlebowski.com/p/…](https://newsletter.ethanchlebowski.com/p/pickle-anything-framework-729d) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250712140129/https://newsletter.ethanchlebowski.com/p/pickle-anything-framework-729d))

{ rating="4" image="pickled_red_onions.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Core

- [ ] [Chopped Red Onions]{ ing="chopped-red-onions" }, Cucumber, Bell Peppers, Carrots, Cauliflower, Green Beans, etc.
- [ ] 200 ml [water]{ ing="water" }
- [ ] 200 ml [vinegar]{ ing="vinegar" }
- [ ] 2% salt by by [weight of brine]{ ing="weight-of-brine" }

### (Optional) Flavor Adjusters

- [ ] 1 tsp [sugar]{ ing="sugar" }
- [ ] [Whole spices]{ ing="whole-spices" } (bay leaves, peppercorns, mustard seeds, star anise, etc.)
- [ ] [Herbs]{ ing="herbs" } (dill, tarragon, fennel, etc.)
- [ ] [Garlic cloves]{ ing="garlic-cloves" }, quartered
- [ ] [Jalapeno]{ ing="jalapeno" }, diced

## Recipe

1. Chop the vegetables and fill one or more mason jars. Typically chopped into long thin pieces
1. Bring the [brine]{ ing="weight-of-brine" } to a boil and pour into the jars. Let cool, then cover and store in the fridge for a few hours or overnight before using

   1. Alternatively, skip boiling and let the brine sit for a few days before use
